    "terrainName": "test-town",
    "description": "What: a Friend 'Patrol' (Man Leader + Man 1-3) at (58-70, 80) marches east to (185, 80) through 'Field C', an enemy anti-personnel field it does not know (110-150, 50-110, a mine every 3 m). The lead man sets off a mine: it goes off ONCE (the trigger fires a mine once), he is hurt, the patrol's MineStrike drill halts it - every man BACKS OUT along his own track to the first point outside the field and holds there (MR-5) - and Friend now SUSPECTS the cells round the blast (CE-4624 MS-B1, MS-T1, MS-T2; Minefields MF-5, MF-13 1). Judge: (1) a mine goes off; (2) a man is hurt; (3) the patrol reacts MineStrike; (4) Friend suspects cells of the field; (5) no second mine goes off while the patrol holds; (6) the men back out along their own track (BackOut). Not yet: care in place. ⚠ (2) is red on terrain's AP-mine damage (CE-2446). Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh mf-strike-and-halt"
  },
